WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:27.980
Title streams around the sombrero galaxy show it grew through repeated mergers 30 million light years away. This is Fascinating Frontiers, episode 213. A seven-day exposure from Namibia captured faint title streams around the sombrero galaxy, known as M-104. The structures include a diagonal ring and extended halo stars that point to past collisions. Light from the galaxy takes 30 million years to reach Earth.

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:31.380
The galaxy spans 150,000 light years.

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:36.060
The longer exposure reveals a hairy halo beyond the familiar dust brim.

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:41.740
Next up, gamma ray observations of the inner Milky Way yield stricter upper limits on

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:43.100
dark matter annihilation.

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:48.020
The study constrains possible particle masses and interaction cross sections.

00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:52.080
The limits come from detailed mapping of the Galactic Center region.

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:57.720
Researcher's analyzed gamma ray observations of the inner Milky Way to set new upper limits

00:00:57.720 --> 00:00:59.460
on dark matter annihilation.

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:05.100
An international team found a previously unseen high-energy phase following a compact

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:05.940
star merger.

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:11.100
The observation came from data collected by the XRISM Observatory.

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:15.140
The phase reveals new details about the aftermath of such events.

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:20.560
Ice grains ejected from Enceladus fractures carry varying chemical signatures from the

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:26.300
subsurface ocean. The diversity arises from different formation depths and interaction times

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:32.620
with the water. The grains offer a direct sample of the moon's hidden ocean. AMD is preparing

00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:38.500
its versatile AI core adaptive system on chip for missions lasting up to 15 years in space.

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:44.640
The chip includes radiation tolerant features and high performance processing for onboard autonomy.

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:50.120
Engineers are testing it against the thermal and radiation stresses of long duration orbits.

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:55.040
The design supports extended operations where traditional processors would fail.

00:01:55.640 --> 00:02:00.740
The UAE placed the first satellite of a planned 10 satellite constellation into orbit.

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:09.760
The Technology Innovation Institute completed its first fully home built deep space probe for a 2028 launch toward the asteroid belt.

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:16.640
The probe carries an AI-capable data processing unit with potential uses in Earth observation and defense.

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:20.740
The constellation will support commercial and scientific goals.

00:02:21.380 --> 00:02:26.580
Multiple space agencies are developing small nuclear reactors to power future moon bases.

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:30.860
The designs aim to provide continuous energy through the lunar night.

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:34.920
The reactors would support sustained human presence on the surface.

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:41.960
Engineers are evaluating three booster engine configurations for hot staging on the stretched starship vehicle.

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:48.760
Options include shutting down to 7 engines, throttling 9 engines, or keeping all 13 center

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:50.340
engines at minimum throttle.

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:54.900
The choices affect separation dynamics and boost back burn requirements.

00:02:55.580 --> 00:03:01.420
Picture a rock body the size of a modest city district, yet formed from a single, slow-cooling

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:03.720
magma chamber 600 million years ago.

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:10.440
On Earth, the Sirriaki Massif in Madagascar reached the surface after tectonic forces

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:14.860
is sheared and uplifted the surrounding crust during the assembly of Gondwana.

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:20.440
The same mineral and northocyte makes up the bright lunar highlands that formed more

00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:25.080
than 4 billion years ago when the Moon's global magma ocean crystallized.

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:31.020
Scientists compare the two because lunar samples are limited while terrestrial outcrops let

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:34.520
them study crystal settling and chemical layering at human scale.

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:40.660
The process begins when dense minerals sink, and lighter plagioclase crystals float and

00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:42.140
accumulate into thick layers.

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:47.920
One remaining puzzle is why earth and north of sites appear in discrete massifs, while

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:50.760
the moon produced a planet-wide crust of the same rock.

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:55.520
Researchers continue to examine how the cooling rates and pressures differed between

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:56.220
the two bodies.

00:03:57.160 --> 00:04:02.740
Alaxundrea O'Brien becomes the first university student from Western Australia, chosen for the

00:04:02.740 --> 00:04:08.160
National Indigenous Space Academy. She studies environmental engineering at the University

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:13.920
of Western Australia and will work at the NASA Jet Propulsion Laboratory. Eight First Nation

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:19.080
students are participating this year. She has mentored others through programs including

00:04:19.080 --> 00:04:25.940
the Pauli Farmer Foundation and CSIRO Indigenous Women's STEM Academy. The Western Australian

00:04:25.940 --> 00:04:31.340
students selected for the National Indigenous Space Academy will work on ocean exploration

00:04:31.340 --> 00:04:37.220
vehicles and microorganism research aboard the International Space Station. Her background in

00:04:37.220 --> 00:04:42.960
environmental engineering and mentoring programs gives her a unique perspective on integrating cultural

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:49.580
knowledge with space technology development. The program pairs participants with mentors at NASA's

00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:56.240
Jet Propulsion Laboratory and RAL Space in the United Kingdom. This placement marks the first time

00:04:56.240 --> 00:04:58.820
a student from her home state has joined the cohort.

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:04.520
The experience is expected to shape her future work on sustainable, culturally informed

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:05.680
engineering practices.

00:05:06.420 --> 00:05:10.780
An all Filipino crew completed a simulated analog mission in Batangas.

00:05:11.380 --> 00:05:15.820
President Marcos met the analog astronauts and representatives from the Philippine Space

00:05:15.820 --> 00:05:16.440
Agency.

00:05:17.060 --> 00:05:20.620
The exercise tested procedures for future crewed operations.

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:25.020
The mission advanced local expertise in crewed simulation techniques.

00:05:25.020 --> 00:05:32.620
Friends' VINP produced a documentary on project tech type, the 1960s undersea habitat program

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:34.040
used to train astronauts.

00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:39.360
The film examines how saturation diving techniques supported space mission preparation.

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:43.900
The project demonstrated long-duration living in extreme environments.

00:05:44.680 --> 00:05:49.780
Richard Spolzino describes his goal of pointing to hardware and knowing his work contributed

00:05:49.780 --> 00:05:50.260
to it.

00:05:50.260 --> 00:05:55.260
The interview outlines remaining technical and schedule challenges for Artemis landings.

00:05:55.640 --> 00:06:00.140
He focuses on practical contributions rather than titles or specific missions.

